{"panel_html": "<section class=\"panel rel-scope active\" id=\"panel-container\" data-rel=\"{}\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">Scroll right for more semesters \u2192</div><div class=\"flow-scroll\"><div class=\"flow-container\">\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 1</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-0-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Asian Civilization 1&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Introduction to major themes and events in the histories of China, Korea, Japan, the Indian subcontinent, and Southeast Asia in early times. Considers the developments of ways of thought, the emergence of and interactions among states and empires, and artistic and literary movements. Our goal is to understand the historical forces and transformations shaping Asia before about 1600. This course is the same as HIS and course repeat rules will apply. Students should consult with their major department regarding any restrictions on their degree requirements.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: true, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7903&amp;returnto=1177&quot;, &quot;groups&quot;: [{&quot;requirement_type&quot;: &quot;choice_required&quot;, &quot;group&quot;: &quot;Asian Studies Core - Asian Civilization (choose 1 of 2)&quot;, &quot;courses&quot;: [{&quot;code&quot;: &quot;AS 181LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Asian Civilization 1&quot;}, {&quot;code&quot;: &quot;AS 182LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Asian Civilization II&quot;}]}]}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">full list on click</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Asian Studies Core - Asian Civilization (choose 1 of 2)</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-0-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Language 101\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7903&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Language 101</div><span class=\"box-credits\">5 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-0-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introduction to Asian Studies&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Are you interested in a career related to Asia, or considering studying abroad in Asia? Or maybe you just want to know more about its cultures and histories because your classmates, neighbors, and coworkers are from there? What is Asia, anyway, and who and what should we consider Asian? This class is designed to introduce students to the diversity of Asia and to the resources at UB and beyond for studying Asia and Asian diasporas. Students will develop critical thinking and writing skills while exploring the fields of Asian and Asian-American studies. The class will hear from distinguished UB professors who will discuss the latest research, trends, and resources in the field of Asian and Asian-American studies. Students also will start thinking about the impact of developments in Asia on their career goals and be encouraged to consider study abroad opportunities in Asia.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;1&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AS 101LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Introduction to Asian Studies</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">1 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"or-group\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-0-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Writing and Rhetoric&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;An introduction to research, writing, and rhetorical practices employed in academic and professional contexts. The course examines the operation of genres, the audiences they address, and the purposes they serve. The course focuses on the analysis and development of student writing and rhetorical practice. Assignments include research essays, digital compositions, and oral presentations.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;ENG 105 non-Z Requisite&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">ENG 105LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Writing and Rhetoric</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span><div class=\"box-note\">(may also be completed in a different semester shown)</div></div><div class=\"or-sep\">or</div><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-0-3-1\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-0-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;UB Seminar: a 1- or 3-credit seminar every student completes in their first semester of enrollment, taught by faculty across departments around a &#x27;big idea&#x27; in the discipline. A UB Curriculum core requirement, not specific to this major.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/seminar.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">UB Seminar</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">15 or 16 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 1</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-1-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-1-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Language 102\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7903&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Language 102</div><span class=\"box-credits\">5 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"or-group\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-1-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Writing and Rhetoric&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;An introduction to research, writing, and rhetorical practices employed in academic and professional contexts. The course examines the operation of genres, the audiences they address, and the purposes they serve. The course focuses on the analysis and development of student writing and rhetorical practice. Assignments include research essays, digital compositions, and oral presentations.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;ENG 105 non-Z Requisite&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">ENG 105LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Writing and Rhetoric</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span><div class=\"box-note\">(may also be completed in a different semester shown)</div></div><div class=\"or-sep\">or</div><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-1-2-1\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-1-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Asian Civilization II&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Introduction to major themes and events in the histories of China, Korea, Japan, the Indian subcontinent, and Southeast Asia in recent centuries. Considers the impacts of colonialism and imperialism, the emergence of nationalist and revolutionary movements, decolonization and the Cold War. Our goal is to understand the historical forces and transformations shaping contemporary Asia, the common experiences that different areas of Asia have shared in the recent past, and what distinguishes the histories of particular Asian nations within a comparative perspective. This course is the same as HIS 182 and course repeat rules will apply. Students should consult with their major department regarding any restrictions on their degree requirements.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: true, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7903&amp;returnto=1177&quot;, &quot;groups&quot;: [{&quot;requirement_type&quot;: &quot;choice_required&quot;, &quot;group&quot;: &quot;Asian Studies Core - Asian Civilization (choose 1 of 2)&quot;, &quot;courses&quot;: [{&quot;code&quot;: &quot;AS 181LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Asian Civilization 1&quot;}, {&quot;code&quot;: &quot;AS 182LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Asian Civilization II&quot;}]}]}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">full list on click</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Asian Studies Core - Asian Civilization (choose 1 of 2)</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">14 or 15 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-2-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Language 201\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7903&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Language 201</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-2-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-2-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Math and Quantitative Reasoning: a 4-credit UB Curriculum Foundations requirement, satisfied by one of several approved math, statistics, or precalculus/calculus courses.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/foundations.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Math &amp; Quantitative Reasoning</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-2-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Scientific Literacy and Inquiry: a 7-credit UB Curriculum Foundations requirement (two lecture courses plus a matching 1-credit lab from the same subject area).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/foundations.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Scientific Literacy and Inquiry 1</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-2-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Scientific Literacy and Inquiry: a 7-credit UB Curriculum Foundations requirement (two lecture courses plus a matching 1-credit lab from the same subject area).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/foundations.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Scientific Literacy and Inquiry Lab</div><span class=\"box-credits\">1 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">15 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-3-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-3-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Scientific Literacy and Inquiry: a 7-credit UB Curriculum Foundations requirement (two lecture courses plus a matching 1-credit lab from the same subject area).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/foundations.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Scientific Literacy and Inquiry 2</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-3-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-3-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Language 202\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7903&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Language 202</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"asian-studies-ba__box-3-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Survey of Asian Literature&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course will introduce students to narratives of romance that span Asia\\u2019s wide variety of religious, literary, theatrical, and cinematic traditions. Rather than defining romance by what it contains, we will instead consider what romance as a genre does. Through this approach, it becomes possible to examine why certain narratives were compelling enough to be transmitted across and preserved within a diverse range of cultures and historical periods. Texts include English translations of Sanskrit drama, a Hindi Sufi mystical work, an early Japanese novel, recent Bollywood cinema, Korean television melodramas, and the worldwide Harlequin Romance phenomenon. There are no prerequisites for this class. We will be covering a wide range of materials, and it is essential that students complete assigned readings before class and actively participate in class discussions. All are welcome in this class, regardless of age, race, sexual orientation, gender identity, ability, ethnicity, or religion. I ask that you keep an open mind towards the course materials and be tolerant and respectful of the opinions expressed by your fellow classmates. This course is the same as ENG 222 and course repeat rules will apply. Students should consult with th